 Taman Desa: A serviced residence near Mid Valley with spacious layouts, private lobbies, and close access to schools, malls, and medical facilities.\n  * M Aurora, Old Klang Road: A freehold serviced residence featuring smart home elements, eco-friendly design, and seamless connectivity to highways and the upcoming MRT3.\n\nEach upcoming project reflects Mah Sing’s commitment to delivering quality homes, sustainable designs, and the best property to buy in Malaysia for both homeowners and investors.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - MahSing040724 (https://cdn1.i3investor.com/my/files/st88k/8583_MAHSING/pt/TA/8583_MAHSING_TA_2024-07-04_BUY_2.05_MahSingGroupBhdThirdLandDealin2024_-1671553410.pdf)\nciteturn278search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Mah Sing Group Bhd None | | | TP: RM2.05 (+13.3%) None | TP: RM2.05 (+13.3%) | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- Mah Sing Group Bhd Third Land Deal in 2024 | | | TP: RM2.05 (+13.3%) | Last Traded: RM1.81 | Mah Sing Group Bhd None | | | TP: RM2.05 (+13.3%) | Buy (ESG: ★★★★) | Mah Sing Group Bhd Thiam Chiann Wen | Tel: +603-2167 9615 | cwthiam@ta.com.my | TP: RM2.05 (+13.3%) None | | www.taonline.com.myShare Information Bloomberg Code MSGB MK Stock Code 8583 Listing Main Market Share Cap (mn) 2,560.1 Market Cap (RMmn) 4,633.9 52-wk Hi/Lo (RM) 1.90/0.61 12-mth Avg Daily Vol ('000 shrs) 10,050.4 Estimated Free Float (%) 58.2 Beta 1.1 Major Shareholders (%) Tan Sri Dato' Sri Leong Hoy Kum - 32.5 PNB - 11.5 Bank of Singapore Limited - 6.1 | | --- | --- | --- Share Information | | Share Information Forecast Revision | | Share Information FY24 FY25 Forecast Revision (%) 0.0 0.0 Net profit (RMmn) 222.5 246.6 Consensus 237.5 265.9 TA's / Consensus (%) 93.7 92.7 Previous Rating Buy (Maintained) Consensus TP (RM) 2.03 | | Share Information Financial Indicators | | Share Information FY24 FY25 Net gearing (%) 24.4 29.3 | | Share Information CFPS (sen) P/CFPS (x) ROE (%) ROA (%) NTA/Share (RM) Price/ NTA (x) | (22.0) (6.3) (8.2) (28.7) 5.9 6.3 3.2 3.2 1.5 1.6 1.2 1.2 | Share Information Share Performance (%) | | Share Information Price Change MSGB FBM KLCI 1 mth 20.7 1.2 3 mth 46.0 5.1 6 mth 114.2 10.5 12 mth 194.3 15.7 | |\nHighway, Federal Highway, New Pantai Expressway, Setiawangsa-Pantai \nExpressway, SPRINT Highway, SMART Tunnel, and KL-Seremban Highway. \nThe land is also conveniently situated near Bandar Malaysia. Since its \ndevelopment in the 1970s, Taman Desa, located off Jalan Klang Lama and the \nEast-West Link Expressway, has been sought-after. Its prime location offers \neasy access to the city centre, Mid Valley Megamall, KL Sentral, Bangsar, and \nmajor suburbs like Petaling Jaya and Cheras. \n \nSee Appendix 1 for the location of the land. \n \nMixed development with a potential GDV of RM1.01bn \nAccording to the preliminary plan, the total GDV of the new development, \nwhich will be named M Aspira, is approximately RM1.01bn. I. It is earmarked \nfor a mixed-use development with approximately 1,600 residential units on 3.7 \nacres and approximately 800 units of Residensi Madani on a 2.47-acre site. The \ndevelopment offers three layout options, with indicative sizes of 708 sqft, 858 \nsqft, and 1,008-1,011 sqft, indicatively priced from RM448,800 onwards (or \nRM600-620 psf).  \n \nAligned with the group's quick turnaround strategy, the management plans to \nlaunch an awareness program and registration of interest for the development \nin 3Q24, pending approval from the relevant authorities. M Aspira is designed \nto attract urbanites, first-time homebuyers, and foreign buyers under the \nMalaysia My Second Home (MM2H) program, offering the vibrancy of city living \ncombined with suburban tranquillity. With the new requirement for MM2H \nholders to purchase a house with a minimum value of RM600,000 under the \nSilver category, M Aspira presents a highly attractive option for both local and \nforeign buyers. \n \n \nPage 1 of 4--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProperty & House For Sale in Malaysia | New Project Launch | Mah Sing (https://www.mahsing.com.my/projects/?nocache=1772493636)\nciteturn278search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Image: Mah Sing_M Mira_Entrance_FA (not affected) ... ### M Aspira ... 1,600 sqft\n### M Zenni\n\n### Serviced Residence\n\n#### Batu Maung, Penang\n\n688 SQFT - 1,184 SQFT\n\nFrom RM530,800\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### Ixora Park City\n\n### 2 & 3 Storey Shop Office\n\n#### Pasir Gudang, Johor\n\n22' x 70' | 30' x 70'\n\nFrom RM758,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### M Grand Minori\n\n### Freehold Serviced Residence\n\n#### Taman Pelangi, Johor Bahru\n\n403 - 835 SQFT\n\nFrom RM390,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### M Sinar @ Southville City\n\n### FREEHOLD Serviced Residence\n\n#### Bangi, Selangor\n\n550 - 868 sqft\n\nFrom RM270,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### M Aurora\n\n### Freehold Serviced Residence\n\n#### Old Klang Road\n\n556 SQFT - 1,019 SQFT\n\nFrom RM339,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### Jasmine 2@ Meridin East\n\n### 2-Storey Terrace House\n\n#### Pasir Gudang, Johor\n\n22'x70' | 1,849 – 1,903 sqft\n\nFrom RM565,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### M Legasi\n\n### 2-Storey Terrace House\n\n#### Semenyih, Selangor\n\n20' x 60' | 20' x 65' | 20' x 70'\n\nFrom RM682,800\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### M Aspira\n\n### Serviced Apartment\n\n#### Taman Desa, KL\n\n706 sqft - 1,006 sqft\n\nFrom RM452,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### Allamanda 5 & 6 @ Meridin East\n\n### 2-Storey Terrace House\n\n#### Pasir Gudang, Johor\n\n18' x 65' | 1,676 sqft\n\nFrom RM491,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### M Azura\n\n### Serviced Residence\n\n#### Setapak\n\n700 SQFT - 1,000SQFT\n\nFrom RM381,000\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n### Ferringhi Residence 2\n\n### Condominium\n\n#### Penang Island\n\n1,208 sqft - 1,565 sqft\n\nFrom RM788,584\n\nExplore\n\nREGISTER\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROPERTY\nMAH SING GROUP \n(MSGB MK EQUITY, MAHS.KL) (https://img.pickastock.info/images/data/pdf/2024/07/8583/8583_MAHSING_AMINVEST_2024-07-04_BUY_2.11_MAHSINGGROUPExpectStrongTakeupRateforMAspirainTamanDesa_521210350.pdf)\nciteturn278search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; MAH SING GROUP ... Expect strong takeup rate for M Aspira in Taman Desa ... 1,600\n8.3 \nMajor Shareholders \nMayang Teratai  (26.2%) \nAmanah Saham Nasional  (11.8%) \nBank of Singapore  (7.3%) \nFree Float \n54.7 \nAvg Daily Value (RMmil) \n25.5 \nPrice performance \n3mth \n6mth \n12mth \n \n \n \nAbsolute (%) \n44.4 \n118.3 \n191.1 \nRelative (%) \n39.8 \n98.5 \n150.8 \n \n1.8\n1,800\n1.6\n1,600\n1.4\n1,400\n1.2\n1,200\n1.0\n1,000\n0.8\n800\n0.6\n600\n0.4\n400\n0.2\n200\n0.0\n0\nJul-19\nJul-20\nJul-21\nJul-22\nJul-23\nMSGB MK\nFBMKLCI Index\n \n  \n• \nWe maintain BUY on Mah Sing Group (Mah Sing) with a higher \nSOP-based fair value (FV) of RM2.11/share (from RM2.09/share \npreviously) to account for the new quick turnaround mixed-\ndevelopment project called M Aspira, which will carry a \nsubstantive GDV of RM1.01bil.  \n• \nOur FV is based on a 30% discount to our SOP-based valuation \n(Exhibit 5) without any changes to a neutral 3-star ESG rating \n(Exhibit 6). The FV implies a FY25F PE of 19x, near its 4-year \npeak. \n• \nWe have also raised FY25F-FY26F earnings by 4%-6% to \naccount for the rapid contribution from M Aspira, scheduled to \nbe open for registration of interest within the next 2 months \neven though the acquisition of the 6.2-acre leasehold land in \nTaman Desa (Exhibit 1: Location Map) from Datuk Bandar Kuala \nLumpur is expected to be completed in 1H2025. \n• \nThe acquisition land cost of RM108mil at RM400 psf is fair given \nthat bungalow land in the township is being offered at RM360-\nRM450 psf currently. This also translates to a reasonable land \ncost reaching only 11% of GDV, at the low end of industry’s \n10%-25%. \n• \nM Aspira’s mixed-use development, envisioned over 4-5 years, \nwill feature 1,600 residential units on 3.7 acres and 800 units of \nResidensi Madani on a 2.47-acre site with a bumi quota of 40%. \nThe indicative sizes of the units are 708 sq ft, 858 sq ft, and \n1,008-1,011 sq ft, indicatively priced at the mid-range affordable \nM-series segment starting from RM448,800 at an attractive \nRM600-RM630 psf. For comparison, the RM700 psf for the \nrecently launched The Atas condominium, also on leasehold \nland in Taman Desa by Exim Global, registered a remarkable \n70% booking during its soft launch in May this year. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMah Sing Group Berhad (https://www.midf.com.my/sites/corporate/files/2024-07/mah_sing_group-cu-land_acquisition_in_taman_desa-midf-040724.pdf)\nciteturn278search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Mah Sing proposed to develop a mixed-use development to be named M Aspira on the land with estimated GDV of RM1.01b, featuring approximately 1,600 residential units on 3.7 acres land and 800 units of Residensi Madani on a 2.47 acres land.\nThe land acquisition is expected to complete in 1HCY25.\n\nM-series project on Taman Desa land. We are positive on the land acquisition as the land acquisition is in line with Mah Sing’s strategy of building affordable M-series projects within Klang Valley. The land is strategically located in Taman Desa with access of multiple expressways and wide range of amenities such as Mid Valley Megamall and KL Eco City. Mah Sing proposed to develop a mixed-use development to be named M Aspira on the land with estimated GDV of RM1.01b, featuring approximately 1,600 residential units on 3.7 acres land and 800 units of Residensi Madani on a 2.47 acres land. Indicative sizes are ranging from 708 sqft to 1,011 sqft with affordable selling price that starts from RM448k. Meanwhile, land cost to GDV ratio is attractive at 11%. Mah Sing targets to start registration of interest in 3QFY24, in line with its quick turnaround strategy.\n\nLow net gearing. Mah Sing intends to fund the acquisition through a combination of internally generated funds and bank borrowings. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBUY \nInvestment Idea \nMah Sing Group Bhd \nEmbarkin (https://cdn1.i3investor.com/my/files/st88k/8583_MAHSING/pt/RAKUTEN/8583_MAHSING_RAKUTEN_2024-08-05_BUY_2.23_MahSingGroupBhdEmbarkingIntoTechrelatedSegment_-494435394.pdf)\nciteturn278search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.2 years ago; Mah Sing Group Bhd ... executed in two phases: M Aspira, featuring around 1,600 residential\nBUY \nInvestment Idea \nMah Sing Group Bhd \nEmbarking into tech-related segment \n           Price: \n   RM1.74 \nTarget price: \n   RM2.23 \nBy Thong Pak Leng, Vice President of Research \nMah Sing Group Berhad (MAHSING, 8583) continues to solidify its \nposition as a leading property developer in Malaysia, with a \ndiversified portfolio. Recently, the company has made significant \nstrides by venturing into the data centre (DC) industry, underscoring \nits commitment to innovation and growth. Based on our estimates, \nthe data centre business is expected to contribute RM60m EBITDA \nfor MAHSING in FY26. BUY with a target price of RM2.23 based on \nSOP (Sum of Parts) valuations. \nIn July 2024, MAHSING acquired 6.17 acres of prime land in Taman \nDesa, Kuala Lumpur, for RM108m. The development, estimated to have \na gross development value (GDV) of approximately RM1.01bn, will be \nexecuted in two phases: M Aspira, featuring around 1,600 residential \nunits on 3.7 acres, and Residensi Madani, with approximately 800 units \non 2.47 acres. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROPERTY\nMAH SING GROUP \n(MSGB MK EQUITY, MAHS.KL) (https://cdn1.i3investor.com/my/files/st88k/8583_MAHSING/pt/AMINVEST/8583_MAHSING_AMINVEST_2024-07-04_BUY_2.11_MAHSINGGROUPExpectStrongTakeupRateforMAspirainTamanDesa_521210350.pdf)\nciteturn278search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; MAH SING GROUP ... Expect strong takeup rate for M Aspira in Taman Desa ... 1,600\npeak. \n• \nWe have also raised FY25F-FY26F earnings by 4%-6% to \naccount for the rapid contribution from M Aspira, scheduled to \nbe open for registration of interest within the next 2 months \neven though the acquisition of the 6.2-acre leasehold land in \nTaman Desa (Exhibit 1: Location Map) from Datuk Bandar Kuala \nLumpur is expected to be completed in 1H2025. \n• \nThe acquisition land cost of RM108mil at RM400 psf is fair given \nthat bungalow land in the township is being offered at RM360-\nRM450 psf currently. This also translates to a reasonable land \ncost reaching only 11% of GDV, at the low end of industry’s \n10%-25%. \n• \nM Aspira’s mixed-use development, envisioned over 4-5 years, \nwill feature 1,600 residential units on 3.7 acres and 800 units of \nResidensi Madani on a 2.47-acre site with a bumi quota of 40%. \nThe indicative sizes of the units are 708 sq ft, 858 sq ft, and \n1,008-1,011 sq ft, indicatively priced at the mid-range affordable \nM-series segment starting from RM448,800 at an attractive \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMah Sing Group Berhad (https://www.midf.com.my/sites/corporate/files/2024-12/mah_sing_group-vn-visit_to_m_aspira_in_taman_desa-midf-051224.pdf)\nciteturn278search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; We recently visited Mah Sing’s M Aspira project in Taman Desa. ... Meanwhile, M Aspira has a total of 1,600 units spread over two towers.\nThe project was launched in mid of November 2024, barely four months after the announcement of land acquisition in July 2024, in line with Mah Sing’s quick turnaround strategy. Recall that Mah Sing signed sale and purchase agreement in July 2024 for acquisition of 6.17 acres of land in Taman Desa for RM108m. The total GDV for the project on Taman Desa land (M Aspira and Residensi Madani) is RM1.01b. Note that Residensi Madani is a one-tower apartment on 2.47 acres of land with total of 800 units and selling price of RM200k for build-up of 800 sq ft. Meanwhile, M Aspira has a total of 1,600 units spread over two towers. The build-up sizes are 708sf, 858sf and 1,011sf with selling price starts from RM448k.\n\nStrong buying interest. M Aspira received 3,000 registrations of interest for M Aspira which could be due to the good location of the project which is just ~5km away from Mid Valley. Demand for affordable residential projects in Klang Valley remains strong due to proximity to KL with easy access for work, shopping and entertainment. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTake Up Rate Of M Projects A Boon For Mah Sing (https://www.businesstoday.com.my/2024/12/05/take-up-rate-of-m-projects-a-boon-for-mah-sing/)\nciteturn278search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; The M Aspira project, launched in November 2024, is part of Mah Sing’s M-series and underscores its swift project development capabilities. ... Residensi Madani offers 800 units with a starting price of RM200,000 for an 800-square-foot build-up, while M Aspira includes 1,600 units across two towers, with sizes ranging from 708 to 1,011 square feet and prices starting at RM448,000.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBERNAMA - Mah Sing To Acquire Dbkl Land For Rm108 Mln (https://www.bernama.com/en/news.php?id=2313934)\nciteturn278search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; In a filing with Bursa Malaysia, Mah Sing Group said the proposed development on the land is expected to have an estimated gross development value of RM1.01 billion and will proceed in two phases.The project, named M Aspira, will comprise approximately 1,600 residential units across 1.50 hectares, and an additional 800 units of Residensi Madani on a one-hectare site within Taman Desa, located off Jalan Klang Lama and the East-West Link Expressway.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMah Sing Acquiring Land In Taman Desa To Build 1600 Residential Unit With GDV Of RM1.01 Billion (https://www.businesstoday.com.my/2024/07/03/mah-sing-acquiring-land-in-taman-desa-for-1600-residential-unit-with-gdv-of-rm1-01-billion/)\nciteturn278search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Phase one will feature M Aspira, a mixed-use development spanning approximately 1,600 residential units across 3.7 acres. ... He underscored Mah Sing’s commitment to integrating green features into M Aspira, promoting sustainability through energy-efficient building practices and enhanced living conditions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMah Sing acquires land in Taman Desa, KL for RM108mil | The Star (https://www.thestar.com.my/business/business-news/2024/07/03/mah-sing-acquires-land-in-taman-desa-kl-for-rm108mil)\nciteturn278search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; With an estimated gross development value (GDV) of approximately RM1.01bil, Mah Sing said the land will be developed in two phases, featuring M Aspira, a mixed-use development with approximately 1,600 residential units on 3.7 acres and approximately 800 units of Residensi Madani on 2.47 acres.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMah Sing acquires KL land for RM108mil | The Star (https://www.thestar.com.my/business/business-news/2024/07/04/mah-sing-acquires-kl-land-for-rm108mil)\nciteturn278search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; With an estimated gross development value (GDV) of RM1.01bil, Mah Sing said the land will be developed in two phases, featuring M Aspira, a mixed-use project with appr